-a list for Milos, Greece-

A stunning island in the Cyclades group (of Santorini and Mykonos), this gem is one of the most beautiful places I have been. The natural volcanic geological formations, the beaches, crystal clear water and the colorful fishing villages, Milos is amazing!

-things to know- • Rent a car • Most beaches are clothing-optional, especially the more remote ones
• Much of the island is protected & you can only see it by boat
• Milos has an airport with flights to/from Athens
• Milos is more about its natural beauty and beaches than it is nightlife, shopping or dining

-activities- • Explore the moon-like landscape at Sarakiniko • Visit the fisherman villages: Klima, Mandrakia & Firopotamos • Watch the sunset from the castle or church in Plaka • Boat around the island to see Kleftiko (Polco Sailing for a fun group experience or rent your own!)
• Rent an ATV • Sip wine in a cave at Kostantakis Winery
• See the ancient ruins

-beaches-
Firiplaka: kayak rentals, sun beds & more 
Firopotamos: fishing village background 
Kalamos: accessible by boat only
Paleochori: colorful cliffs
Tsigrado: access by ladder, coves & stunning water 

